From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x86-power-control: expose force-off pulse while host is off

The BIOS update CPLD handoff can already put the host in S5 before the BMC
finishes flashing. In that state a normal Off transition is a no-op, but the
board requires one explicit 15-second power-button override before powering
the host back on. Expose a guarded board-used method while preserving GPIO
ownership in x86-power-control.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board-specific power sequence]
---
 src/power_control.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/power_control.cpp b/src/power_control.cpp
--- a/src/power_control.cpp
+++ b/src/power_control.cpp
@@ -3211,3 +3211,18 @@
     chassisIface->register_property("CurrentPowerState",
                                     std::string(getChassisState(powerState)));
+    chassisIface->register_method("ForcePowerButtonOff", []() {
+        if (powerState != PowerState::off)
+        {
+            throw std::invalid_argument("ForcePowerButtonOff requires host Off");
+        }
+        if (powerButtonMask)
+        {
+            throw std::invalid_argument("Power button output is masked");
+        }
+        if (assertGPIOForMs(powerOutConfig, TimerMap["ForceOffPulseMs"]) < 0)
+        {
+            throw std::runtime_error("Failed to assert force-off power button");
+        }
+        lg2::info("Force-off power-button pulse started while host is Off");
+    });
     chassisIface->register_property("LastStateChangeTime", getCurrentTimeMs());
